The important difference: your old highlighter did this:

html = html.replace(...)
html = html.replace(...)
html = html.replace(...)

so after the first replacement it was trying to syntax-highlight the <span class="str">...</span> markup it had already created. That’s why your code could look plain, broken, or have weird nested colors.

The new version sends the original raw code directly to Prism once, so you get proper C++, C-style comments, strings, numbers, keywords, functions, and Luau highlighting without the regex collision.
